# Terraform IaC control plane

Phase 7 of the multi-tenant rollout — see
[aqp_docs/terraform-control-plane.md](mdc:aqp_docs/terraform-control-plane.md)
for the narrative walkthrough. AGENTS rules 42 + 43 in
[AGENTS.md](mdc:AGENTS.md) are the source of truth.

## Hard rules

1. **All Terraform lifecycle actions go through
   [`TerraformRuntime`](mdc:aqp/terraform/runtime.py)** (rule 42).
   Routes / Celery tasks / MCP tools wrap it; nothing calls
   `subprocess.run(["terraform", ...])` directly outside
   [`aqp/terraform/runner.py::TerraformExecutor`](mdc:aqp/terraform/runner.py).
2. **`terraform_stack_spec_versions` rows are immutable hash-locked
   snapshots** (rule 43). Re-snapshotting via
   [`aqp/terraform/registry.py::persist_spec`](mdc:aqp/terraform/registry.py)
   inserts a new row when the SHA-256 changes; existing rows are
   append-only.
3. **CDKTF was deprecated by HashiCorp on 2025-12-10. Python-side
   HCL generation uses Jinja2 templates** under
   [`aqp/terraform/codegen/templates/`](mdc:aqp/terraform/codegen/templates).
   New module-kind support = new `.tf.j2` template + matching emit
   path in [`aqp/terraform/codegen/base.py`](mdc:aqp/terraform/codegen/base.py).
4. **`TerraformRun` carries `experiment_id` + `test_id`** (rule 34).
   The runtime stamps from the constructor's `experiment_id` arg;
   callers populate via :class:`RequestContext` and route through
   :func:`aqp.terraform.runtime.TerraformRuntime` directly.
5. **The runner pod has two SA flavors** — `aqp-terraform-readonly`
   for `plan`, `aqp-terraform-writer` for `apply`. The kill-switch
   secret is mounted as tmpfs (never persisted to disk).
6. **Five state backends are supported**: `local | s3 | azurerm | gcs |
   hcp`. The HCP path uses
   [`aqp/terraform/hcp_client.py`](mdc:aqp/terraform/hcp_client.py)
   (thin httpx wrapper around `app.terraform.io/api/v2`); no
   `python-terrasnek` dep so cold installs without HCP credentials
   still boot cleanly.
7. **Frontend Terraform pages live under `/infra/terraform/*`**
   (Vite, not legacy webui). Plan / apply / destroy actions are
   friction-gated via
   [`ConfirmFrictionDialog`](mdc:aqp_client/src/components/common/ConfirmFrictionDialog.tsx).

## Don't

- Don't import :mod:`aqp.persistence.models_terraform` from an agent
  body. Agents go through `data.terraform.*` MCP tools (rule 22).
- Don't run `terraform apply` against state files outside the
  `AQP_TERRAFORM_WORKSPACES_DIR/<workspace_id>/` directory. The
  runner is the only sanctioned executor.
- Don't author module HCL in Python `f"..."` strings. Use Jinja2
  templates so the rendered output is reviewable.
- Don't bypass the `/terraform/halt` fan-out target in the topbar
  `KillSwitch`. Every long-running runtime is in the halt list
  (rule applies to new runtimes too).
- Don't put secret values into the rendered HCL. Every secret lands
  via `ExternalSecret` -> `ClusterSecretStore` -> Vault / cloud
  secret manager.

